                <head>229. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>Delegations from the United States and the United Kingdom, led by President
                    Eisenhower and Prime Minister Macmillan, respectively, met at Bermuda for a
                    3-day conference, March 21–23, in order to discuss matters of mutual concern.
                    Extensive documentation on these <pb facs="0571" n="543" xml:id="pg543"/> talks,
                    which includes discussion of European integration, is scheduled for publication
                    in a forthcoming <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi> volume.</p>
            </div>
